An iOS window is the screen -- in points.

Two things about the window are wrong on iOS. It asks to be resizable and not
fullscreen, and a window there cannot be either: it is the screen.

The third would have been ALLOW_HIGHDPI, and it is a trap. The engine takes its
backbuffer size from SDL_GL_GetDrawableSize (renderer/backend/gl/Device.cpp) and
its viewport from g_xres/g_yres, which come from SDL_GetWindowSize -- pixels on
one side, points on the other. Everywhere those two agree the mix is harmless.
On a 3x screen with ALLOW_HIGHDPI they differ by three, and the game draws into
one ninth of the frame at the origin.

That is not a guess: the first screenshot after the port drew anything shows the
whole interface inside a 393x853 block of a 1179x2556 capture, one ninth, flush
against the corner -- and rotating that block 90 degrees counter-clockwise gives
an upright main menu. Which incidentally settles a second question: the
simulator *does* rotate the app to landscape, it simply captures in the device's
native portrait.

--- source/ps/VideoMode.cpp
+++ source/ps/VideoMode.cpp
@@ -396,6 +396,20 @@
 		flags |= SDL_WINDOW_SHOWN | SDL_WINDOW_RESIZABLE;
 		if (m_ConfigEnableHiDPI)
 			flags |= SDL_WINDOW_ALLOW_HIGHDPI;
+#if OS_IOS
+		// An iOS window is the screen: it cannot be resized, and it is always
+		// fullscreen.
+		//
+		// And it must not ask for ALLOW_HIGHDPI, however tempting that looks.
+		// The engine takes its backbuffer size from SDL_GL_GetDrawableSize
+		// (Device.cpp) and its viewport from g_xres/g_yres, which come from
+		// SDL_GetWindowSize (below) -- pixels and points. They are equal
+		// everywhere those two agree; with ALLOW_HIGHDPI on a 3x screen they
+		// differ by three, and the game renders into one ninth of the frame at
+		// the origin. That is measurable: 852x393 of a 2556x1179 buffer.
+		flags &= ~static_cast<Uint32>(SDL_WINDOW_RESIZABLE | SDL_WINDOW_ALLOW_HIGHDPI);
+		flags |= SDL_WINDOW_FULLSCREEN;
+#endif
 		if (isGLBackend)
 			flags |= SDL_WINDOW_OPENGL;
 		else if (m_Backend == Renderer::Backend::Backend::VULKAN)
